1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,187
The Rainy Walk Home.

3
00:00:03,187 --> 00:00:07,052
School ends, and rain is falling hard outside the front doors.

4
00:00:07,052 --> 00:00:08,979
Emma opens her umbrella.

5
00:00:08,979 --> 00:00:13,490
I open my backpack and find a notebook, a snack, and no umbrella at all.

6
00:00:13,706 --> 00:00:15,198
Do you want to share my umbrella?

7
00:00:15,484 --> 00:00:17,165
Yes, please.

8
00:00:17,165 --> 00:00:20,269
Mine is doing an excellent job of staying dry at home.

9
00:00:20,269 --> 00:00:25,071
We step outside together and immediately discover that walking under one umbrella takes teamwork.

10
00:00:25,298 --> 00:00:26,842
You're getting wet on that side.

11
00:00:26,842 --> 00:00:28,102
Come a little closer.

12
00:00:28,372 --> 00:00:29,959
I move closer.

13
00:00:29,959 --> 00:00:31,689
Our backpacks bump.

14
00:00:31,689 --> 00:00:34,032
We take three steps and bump again.

15
00:00:34,032 --> 00:00:37,793
After a minute, we find a rhythm that doesn't involve walking into each other.

16
00:00:38,018 --> 00:00:39,926
Should we take the shortcut through the park?

17
00:00:40,204 --> 00:00:41,979
Let's take the longer way.

18
00:00:41,979 --> 00:00:45,927
The path gets muddy, and I don't want to bring half the park home on my shoes.

19
00:00:46,154 --> 00:00:47,021
Good point.

20
00:00:47,021 --> 00:00:48,219
Sidewalk it is.

21
00:00:48,508 --> 00:00:51,304
At the corner, we stop before a giant puddle.

22
00:00:51,304 --> 00:00:54,325
I go around the left side while Emma starts going right.

23
00:00:54,325 --> 00:00:56,814
The umbrella can't decide who to follow.

24
00:00:57,050 --> 00:00:58,260
Same side, Lucy.

25
00:00:58,260 --> 00:00:59,958
We need to choose the same side.

26
00:01:00,244 --> 00:01:01,352
Right.

27
00:01:01,352 --> 00:01:04,050
This is more complicated than our group project.

28
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:06,623
We laugh and carefully walk around together.

29
00:01:06,623 --> 00:01:10,081
When we reach my house, Mom opens the door with a towel.

30
00:01:10,348 --> 00:01:12,165
Come in, both of you.

31
00:01:12,165 --> 00:01:14,300
You look like you've had an adventure.

32
00:01:14,572 --> 00:01:17,076
A very small, very wet adventure.

33
00:01:17,076 --> 00:01:19,837
Tomorrow, my umbrella is coming to school.

34
00:01:19,837 --> 00:01:21,962
It has enjoyed enough time off.
